1
00:00:01,600 --> 00:00:04,800
This customer's fixed rate ends in March.

2
00:00:05,400 --> 00:00:09,600
Without a moment, the first anyone hears
is the redemption notice.

3
00:00:10,400 --> 00:00:15,600
Parcelwise reads their customer data,
the property and the market together.

4
00:00:16,400 --> 00:00:21,000
Out of 40,000 customers, they're third
on this week's list.

5
00:00:21,800 --> 00:00:26,000
The biggest reason: the market rate
is 1.7 points above their contract.

6
00:00:26,200 --> 00:00:30,600
Equity, local offers and the reset date
make up the rest, adding up to 100.

7
00:00:31,400 --> 00:00:36,600
The advisor gets the call in the CRM,
with every reason attached.

8
00:00:37,600 --> 00:00:41,600
Tested on a past book first,
so you know what the ranking is worth.

9
00:00:42,400 --> 00:00:45,800
See what your own book holds.

